# Safety and claims

Never diagnose, recommend treatment, replace clinicians, or display “Patient has disease X.”

Frame outputs as **measured sensory characteristics**, not diagnosis.

Never:

- Claim clinical validation or that an algorithm is clinically superior without experimental evidence
- Invent medical reference ranges or hard-code arbitrary medical values
- Direct users into unsafe oral / chemical / thermal experiments
- Pretend a phone physically measures sensation
- Present prototype results as clinical conclusions
- Fake datasets or circular validation (fit the algorithm to a paper’s final number)

The hackathon adaptive engine is a **technical prototype**, not clinically validated software.

If using synthetic data, label it, e.g.:

> Synthetic validation dataset generated using published test parameters. Demonstrates the analysis engine and adaptive workflow; this is not clinical validation.

Never present synthetic data as real patient data. If no public raw dataset exists, say so.
